Z||000005||fyerstarter||04-08-2001||02:41 PM||||The sad truth is that most rice-boy cars in stock form will beat your Fiero in stock form 9 times out of 10. Does that make me love my Fiero any less? Of course not. You complain about the riceboys bolting on useless accesorries such as a rear-wing on a front wheel drive car. Well maybe someone can explain to me then the usefullness of all these hood scoops that I have seen on Fieros? The most common excuse seems to be "it aids cooling". Well does your Fiero run hot now? Are you constantly overheating? I think not. Cooler does not = better or more horsepower. The engine was made to run at a normal operating temperature and the stock cooling system does a fine job of keeping it within this range. How about all the people with the stock air intake setup and side scoops? That is the equivalent of ramming air into a brick wall!<P>Now I came from the import scene to Fieros and I hate the latest sticker fad and the attitude which has given import tuning a bad name. But I see a lot of the same from the camaro people and the fiero people. I love all cars if they are done right, low-riders, muscle cars, 4x4's, imports, fiero's, whatever. <P>Wouldn't it be nice if car guys could quit being "Chevy guys" and "Ford guys" and just respect this sport for what it is. ||||reg||1
