Z||000026||fyerstarter||04-10-2001||12:54 AM||||God this discussion gets old. <P>First take your stock intake out of the car and examine the sound resonator/water filter box, it is located between the air intake vent on the side of the car and the filter canister. <P>Now you will notice that about half an inch inside the the air inlet is a plastic fence with a hole the side of a flathead screwdriver in it, reach your hand up around the top and you will feel how the air is directed over this fence and then back down before heading through the tube up to the filter cannister.<P>Now if you know anything about momentum at all you will realize that no matter how hard you "ram air" into the stock intake system it "rams" head on into this fence. Then it will continue above the fence and through the maze of restrictions/filters until it finally reaches the throttle body at the same rate as it would have without scoops.||||reg||1
